      "title": "CRK",
      "topic": "The Work of the Holy Spirit",
      "dates": "September 21 – 25, 2026",
      "content": "it\n\n• Bible Reference: John 14:26, John 16:13, Acts 2:1–11\n\n• Behavioral Objectives: By the end of the lesson, pupils should be able to list at least three roles\n\nof the Holy Spirit and explain how He helps children make good choices.\n\n• Instructional Materials: Flashcards showing actions like praying, reading the Bible, helping\n\nothers.\n\nLesson Content\n\nThe Holy Spirit is not a ghost or a wind; He is God living inside the hearts of believers. Because He lives inside us, He performs many wonderful works every single day to help us grow as children of God. His\n\nmajor works include:\n\n1. Teaching and Reminding: Sometimes, we read the Bible or hear a sermon in Sunday School\n\nbut do not fully understand it. The Holy Spirit acts as an invisible teacher in our hearts, explaining God's word to us. He also reminds us of what we have learned when we are about to make a\n\nmistake.\n\n2. Guiding Us: The Holy Spirit is like a spiritual GPS or compass. He leads us into all truth. When\n\nwe are about to tell a lie, join bad gangs, or disobey our parents, we hear a gentle, quiet voice in our minds telling us, \"Don't do that; it is wrong.\" That is the Holy Spirit guiding us.\n\n3. Giving Courage and Power: Before the Holy Spirit came, the disciples were hiding in a locked\n\nroom because they were afraid. After He came, they stood boldly in the streets to preach. He gives children the boldness to stand up for what is right, even if their friends are doing wrong.\n\n4. Producing Good Fruit: The Holy Spirit helps us to be loving, joyful, peaceful, patient, kind, and\n\nself-controlled (Galatians 5:22-23).\n\nTeacher & Learner Activities\n\n• Teacher: Discusses everyday situations where pupils need the Holy Spirit's guidance (e.g.,\n\nfinding a lost item, deciding not to cheat on a test).\n\n• Learners: Share personal examples of times they felt a quiet voice telling them to do good.\n\nAssessment & Homework\n\n• Evaluation: Name three things the Holy Spirit does for believers. How does the Holy Spirit help\n\nus when we are afraid?\n\n• Assignment: Draw a picture of a child praying and write \"Holy Spirit, guide me.\""
